{title: 078 - For God So Loved Us}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #078 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 78}
{meta: category God the Father - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]For God so loved us,
[D]He [Bm]sent the [G]Savior:
[D]For God so [A7/E]loved us,
[A7]and loves me too.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[D]Love so [A7/E]unending!
[A7]I'll sing His [D]praises,
[A7/E]God loves His children,
[D]loves even me.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]He sent the Savior,
[D]the [Bm]blest Redeemer;
[D]He sent the [A7/E]Savior
[A7]to set me free.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]He bade me welcome,
[D]O [Bm]word of [G]mercy;
[D]He bade me [A7/E]welcome,
[A7]O voice divine.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[D]Glory and honor,
[D]O [Bm]Love eternal,
[D]To Him be [A7/E]given
[A7]while life shall last.
{end_of_verse}
